  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Wilfrid Dewhurst Wills was a British Member of Parliament for Batley and Morley from 1931 to 1935. He was born in Bromley, Kent, and attended Cheltenham College and the Royal Military College, Sandhurst, for officer training. His father, Arthur Stanley Wills, was a barrister and director of the family's tobacco business.",
    "html": "<p>Wilfrid Dewhurst Wills was a British Member of Parliament for Batley and Morley from 1931 to 1935. He was born in Bromley, Kent, and attended Cheltenham College and the Royal Military College, Sandhurst, for officer training. His father, Arthur Stanley Wills, was a barrister and director of the family's tobacco business.</p>\r\n",
