  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "British parliamentarian Wilfrid Wills took an interest in the practical arrangements that brought overseas buyers to British manufacturers. He asked ministers to ensure a suitable welcome for a visiting delegation of Swiss businesspeople at the British Industries Fair. The response outlined invitations to the opening banquet and reception plans in Birmingham.\n\nMilitary service took him into two different branches of the armed forces. He held a lieutenant's commission in the 5th Dragoon Guards during the First World War. During the Second World War, he served as a lieutenant-commander in the Royal Naval Volunteer Reserve.",
    "html": "<p>British parliamentarian Wilfrid Wills took an interest in the practical arrangements that brought overseas buyers to British manufacturers. He asked ministers to ensure a suitable welcome for a visiting delegation of Swiss businesspeople at the British Industries Fair. The response outlined invitations to the opening banquet and reception plans in Birmingham.</p>\r\n<p>Military service took him into two different branches of the armed forces. He held a lieutenant's commission in the 5th Dragoon Guards during the First World War. During the Second World War, he served as a lieutenant-commander in the Royal Naval Volunteer Reserve.</p>\r\n",
